{#
  apt takes the first stanza that matches a version:
  - Ubuntu's varnish packages are never installed;
  - Varnish Software's versions of the series win (with or without an epoch);
  - any other version (another series) is never installed.
  Without Varnish Software's package lists there is no candidate, and the
  install fails instead of falling back to Ubuntu's varnish.
#}
Explanation: managed by noixdev.infra (varnish role). Changes here are overwritten.
Package: {{ varnish_apt_packages }}
Pin: release o=Ubuntu
Pin-Priority: -1

Package: {{ varnish_apt_packages }}
Pin: version /^([0-9]+:)?{{ varnish_version | regex_escape }}\./
Pin-Priority: 990

Package: {{ varnish_apt_packages }}
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1
